    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm hitting a massive headache with our jenkins pipeline. we've got these intermittent failures during the unit test stage in our CI/CD flow. the code hasn't changed, but the builds are just... flaky. sometimes it passes, sometimes it fails with weird timeout errors or random asset loading failures. it's non-deterministic as hell. how can i start isolating whether this is an env issue or something in the container orchestration?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To isolate the source of your intermittent failures, start by running your unit tests outside of the Jenkins pipeline using a local environment or a container like Docker, to ensure the issue isn't specific to the CI/CD environment. Then, try running your pipeline again while passing in environment variables or setting the same configuration that you have in the pipeline to see if it makes a difference. This can help you determine if it's an issue with your container or the underlying orchestration. Additionally, consider reducing the complexity of your pipeline and focus on one stage at a time to help you identify where the failure might be more consistently occurring.",
